# Maven Doxia

Doxia is the document engine behind every Maven site. It reads the pages you write in Markdown, APT, Xdoc, FML or
XHTML and the reports that plugins generate, and turns them into HTML. When you run `mvn site`, the
[Maven Site Plugin](/plugins/maven-site-plugin/) uses Doxia to do the work.

The current release of [Doxia](./doxia/) is ${doxiaVersion}.

<a id="Doxia_Reference_Pages"></a>

${esc.h}${esc.h} Write a site

You don't need to install or configure Doxia: the Maven Site Plugin includes every format listed here. Put your
pages under `src/site/<format>/` and run `mvn site`. The [guide to creating a site](/guides/mini/guide-site.html)
covers the whole setup.

- [Choose a format](./references/index.html). Markdown is the best choice for new pages. APT and Xdoc still work,
  and [Migrating APT to Markdown](./migrating-apt-to-markdown.html) shows how to move existing pages. FML is
  deprecated since Doxia 2.2.0.
- [Add generated content with macros](./macros/index.html), such as a table of contents (`toc`) or a code
  excerpt from a source file (`snippet`).
- [Draw diagrams with Mermaid](./mermaid-diagrams.html).
- [Check what each format can and cannot express](./references/index.html#Limitations) before you convert a page.
- If something renders differently from what you expect, see the [FAQ](./faq.html) and
  [Issues and Gotchas](./issues/index.html).

${esc.h}${esc.h} Write a plugin report or extend Doxia

Report plugins write their output through the Doxia Sink API, which keeps them independent of the output format.

- [Using the Sink API](./developers/sink.html) shows how to emit headings, tables and links.
- [Creating a Doxia Macro](./developers/macros.html) and [Creating a Doxia Module](./developers/modules.html) show
  how to add your own macro or markup format.
- The [Overview](./overview.html) explains how parsers, sinks and the site renderer fit together.

<a id="Main_Features"></a>

${esc.h}${esc.h} Components

Doxia is released as three components.

| Component | What it does |
|---|---|
| [Doxia](./doxia/) | The Sink API, the parsers and sinks for each format, and the macros. |
| [Doxia Sitetools](./doxia-sitetools/) | The site model (`site.xml`) and the renderer that applies a skin to the pages. |
| [Doxia Tools](./doxia-tools/) | Stand-alone tools, such as the [Doxia Converter](./doxia-tools/doxia-converter/index.html), which converts a document from one format to another. |

All components are published to Maven Central under the `org.apache.maven.doxia` group ID, see
[Downloads](./downloads.html).

<a id="Brief_History"></a>

${esc.h}${esc.h} History

Doxia is based on the Aptconvert project by [XMLmind](https://www.xmlmind.com/), was first hosted at
Codehaus, and became a Maven subproject in 2006. Doxia 2.0, released in 2024, moved the output to HTML5 and
removed the PDF, LaTeX, RTF, DocBook, Confluence and TWiki modules; see
[Former Doxia Formats](./references/index.html#Former_Doxia_Formats).
